## Combining Multiple Interface Requirements

### Three Interfaces

```xiom
interface Cloneable {
  fn duplicate(&self) -> Self;
}

interface Printable {
  fn to_text(&self) -> Str;
}

interface Sortable {
  fn comes_before(&self, other: &Self) -> Bool;
}
```

### Requiring All Three

```xiom
fn export_data[T: Cloneable + Printable + Sortable](items: &Vec[T]) {
  let mut sorted = items.clone();  // needs Cloneable
  sort_by_interface(&mut sorted);   // needs Sortable
  let mut i = 0;
  while i < sorted.len() {
    io.println(sorted.get(i).unwrap().to_text());  // needs Printable
    i += 1;
  };
}
```

`T: Cloneable + Printable + Sortable` means: every T passed to this function MUST implement all three interfaces. The compiler enforces this.

### A Type That Satisfies All Three

```xiom
type DataPoint {
  value: Int;
  label: Str;
}

fn DataPoint.duplicate(&self) -> DataPoint {
  DataPoint{ value: self.value, label: self.label.clone() }
}

fn DataPoint.to_text(&self) -> Str {
  self.label.clone()
}

fn DataPoint.comes_before(&self, other: &DataPoint) -> Bool {
  self.value < other.value
}
```

